---
id: pan-seared-roasted-pork-tenderloin
title: Pan-Seared & Roasted Pork Tenderloin
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 3
  cooked_g: 460

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Trim the white silverskin along the loin from @pork-tenderloin{1} using a sharp chef's knife. Pat the meat thoroughly dry on all sides with paper towels so the sear crust adheres.

Rub the tenderloin with 1 tsp of @avocado-oil{1%tbsp}, then coat evenly on all sides with @kosher-salt{1%tsp}, @black-pepper{0.5%tsp}, @smoked-paprika{1%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1%tsp}, and @dried-thyme{0.5%tsp}.

Heat the remaining 2 tsp avocado oil in a #skillet over medium-high heat until shimmering hot. Sear the pork for ~sear-time{7%min}, turning every 90 seconds to brown all sides evenly.

Transfer the seared tenderloin to a rimmed #sheet-pan and roast in the #oven preheated to 200°C (400°F) for ~roast-time{15%min}, pulling it as soon as the core temperature reaches 60°C (140°F) at the thickest part checked with a #meat-thermometer.

Transfer the meat to a cutting board and let rest loosely tented under foil for ~rest-time{8%min}. Meanwhile, return the #skillet to medium heat, add @chicken-broth{0.5%cup}, @dijon-mustard{1%tbsp}, and smashed @fresh-garlic{2%clove}. Simmer for ~reduction-time{3%min}, scraping up the browned fond with a wooden spatula, until reduced by half. Stir in any collected resting juices from the cutting board.

Slice the pork tenderloin against the grain into 1/2-inch medallions. Divide evenly into 3 meal prep containers (~153 g cooked pork medallions each) and spoon the warm pan reduction evenly over the portions.
